sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Listener
  participant UI as Atlas or clock UI
  participant API as /api/recommend
  participant Core as recommendRagas
  participant Clock as praharForMinutes
  participant Seed as RAGAS dataset
  participant Engine as AudioEngine
  participant Rasa as rasa reference service

  Listener->>UI: Open the atlas or move the clock hand
  UI->>API: GET /api/recommend with minutes and limit
  API->>API: Parse and clamp minutes to 0 through 1439
  API->>Core: recommendRagas dataset, minutes, options
  Core->>Clock: Resolve the watch for this minute
  Clock-->>Core: Prahar number 1 through 8
  Core->>Seed: Read prahar, season, rasa, and tags
  Seed-->>Core: Candidate ragas
  Core->>Core: Score same watch 100, adjacent 32, two away 12
  Core->>Core: Add 20 for matching season and 14 for monsoon
  Core->>Core: Sort by score then name and apply the limit
  Core-->>API: ScoredRaga array with reasons
  API-->>UI: JSON response
  UI-->>Listener: Render the top three with explanations

  Listener->>UI: Start the tanpura
  UI->>Engine: Create and resume AudioContext inside the gesture
  Engine-->>UI: Drone running at the chosen Sa
  UI-->>Listener: Unmuted audio, animated meter

  Note over Rasa,Core: Python tests encode the same scoring contract and rank order
  Note over UI,Engine: Mute ramps master gain to zero without rebuilding the graph
